d |\\{w \\mid w \\in d\\}|\n$$\n\n**Component Breakdown:**\n*   `{w | w ∈ d}`: This is the set of unique word types in document $d$. The set-builder notation gathers every word `w` that appears in document `d` at least once, and the set structure automatically discards all duplicates.\n*   `| ... |`: The cardinality operator is applied to this set, counting the number of unique elements within it.\n\n**B. Lexical Density (LD)**\nA measure of lexical diversity, representing the ratio of unique word types to the total number of word tokens. This value is normalized for document length.\n\n**Formal Definition:**\n$$\n\\text{LD}_d \u003d \\frac{|\\{w \\mid w \\in d\\}|}{N}\n$$\n\n**Component Breakdown:**\n*   $|\\{w \\mid w \\in d\\}|$: The numerator, which is the Unique Word Count (UWC) as defined above.\n*   $N$: The denominator, which is the total number of tokens in document $d$.\n\n**C. Personal Pronoun Proportion (PRP)**\nThe proportion of tokens in a document that are personal pronouns. This is used to gauge the level of subjectivity. Let $P$ be the predefined set of personal pronouns (e.g., \u0027I\u0027, \u0027me\u0027, \u0027we\u0027, \u0027us\u0027, \u0027you\u0027, etc.).\n\n**Formal Definition:**\n$$\n\\text{PRP}_d \u003d \\frac{\\sum_{i\u003d1}^{N} \\mathbb{I}(w_i \\in P)}{N}\n$$\n\n**Component Breakdown:**\n*   $\\sum_{i\u003d1}^{N}$: This sums the results for every single token from the first ($i\u003d1$) to the last ($i\u003dN$).\n*   $w_i$: The token at the $i$-th position. Unlike the set notation in UWC, this preserves duplicates, as each position is evaluated independently.\n*   $\\mathbb{I}(w_i \\in P)$: The indicator function returns 1 if the token $w_i$ is an element of the set of personal pronouns $P$, and 0 otherwise.\n*   The full numerator, $\\sum_{i\u003d1}^{N} \\mathbb{I}(w_i \\in P)$, therefore, is the total count of personal pronoun occurrences in the document.\n*   $N$: The denominator, which normalizes the count to get a proportion.",
